WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.710
Around 1800, a bold new idea spreads: you
can read a person's mind from the bumps

2
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:08.070
on their head.

3
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:10.210
A bump here means kindness.

4
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.590
A bump there means courage.

5
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.670
It was called phrenology.

6
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.070
It claimed each mental ability
had its own brain area,

7
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.340
shown by bumps on the skull.

8
00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:23.900
Today, psychologists
don't feel people's heads.

9
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:26.520
So what replaced reading the skull?

10
00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:30.380
In this mission, you'll meet the
science that took phrenology's place,

11
00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:35.690
cognitive neuroscience, and find out what
it does instead of feeling for bumps.

12
00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.730
You'll trace the story from 1800 to today,

13
00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:42.120
and find out which part
of the old idea lasted.

14
00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:45.790
Your mission: work out what
replaced reading the skull.
